                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The game need an almost full reshape.\nI've played the game for years, reach tier 21, ancient gear and mythic familiars. But i won't invest anymore in this game until the devs do asomething about the main issues :\n- The game take too much of your time daily, could be a good idea to have 1000 energy that you use on every gamemode instead of having 8 variant.\n- Legendary/mythic pets and gears are too annoying to acquire good gear probs need a buff and familiar could  have a 100% chance of recrutment without ruining the economy of the game. All the uptiering mechanic is flawed and should be changed. Uptiering a mythic or ancient gear is almost impossible passed tier 20/21 concidering how expensive it is and how rare the mythic boss world drops are.\n- Speaking of boss world gamemode, it should be playable with your own pets or at least the servers should sort the player who seek the same boss world and tier on the same lobby.\n- Ancient gear are uninstall-the-game-stupid to acquire, you need 2 or 3 tier above the current tier mission to be viable. I'm tier 21 with maxed ancient and set gear maxed mythic pet and i get one-shot-team by the first mob i encounter. Its clearly meant to be a whale bait, as regular player who dont buy stat points cannot do anything.\n- Passed some point the fights are a mess its impossible to understand what damage what. Its almost like their are hidden stats and perks that decide in advance who would win. The game is pretty unbalanced.\n- The game itself is very vain to play, either you auto-farm, aka you do nothing because their are no stategies or you play the ancient difficulty mission where you get one-shot. In every cases you're bored, and you just leave the game for good.\nI guess the devs will never read that but here is a peacefull message from an ex-fan (who could come back) :\nThe game is very good in some way but you cannot look at me in the eye and tell me that you're satisfied with the current state of the game. More and more people are leaving the game and those who stay are falling in the sunk cost fallacy. But more and more people are snapping out of it and the game is slowly dying. The ideas i and the other are giving you are easy to add and could save Bit Heroes. I really miss the game and the good old high school time where i played it. \n",
